text: >-
  Let us draw these ruminations to a close with a series of questions. Did Tyler
  really stay the

  night with Lance on the evening of the 9th? Where was his car? Can this be
  confirmed by

  satellite images? Why did Lance not try to communicate with his missing
  partner throughout the

  day? Was he really following the Charlie Kirk story that afternoon? Did he
  really read the note

  that Tyler allegedly sent? If so, why was he astonished twice by the
  revelation that Tyler was the

  killer? Why did Tyler write as if Lance already knew he was in Orem? Why did
  Lance have to

  ask about Tyler's motivation, and how come he had forgotten about the bullet
  engravings so

  soon? Why did Lance tell the FBI only about the Zealous Monkey surrender and
  not his own

  private text message? How come this was from "Tylor/Ikum"? Why is "Tylor"
  misspelled? Why

  the need to conceal Mike Mitchell? How and when did the FBI first learn about
  Lance? And,

  when and why did they decide to give him immunity? Is Agent Lange taking the
  stand in July?

  Why not?
